+# N25 validation preparation: explicit runner routing addendum v1
+
+This addendum supersedes only the previous requirement that the shared runner remain wholly byte-identical in protocol-validation-conditional-v1.md (SHA5ed12805f71bfb2a727af4489fd1ccc0fcb962b48641679a4ad935e935e1df35). All science, budgets, gates, no-real-data CPU boundary, independent worktree and future adoption requirements remain unchanged.
+
+Root inspected exact frozen runner source and the previous N24 validation diff. New N25 validation plans must keep n25_cohort for unchanged native audit activation, but the frozen runner currently classifies any such plan as Dev and requires its 40-cell contract. A separate validation dispatch implementation would duplicate resource/accounting admission. Permit the same narrow explicit evaluation-routing pattern already reviewed for N24, entirely inside the isolated future validation source; current W/Dev source remains untouched.
+
+Permitted shared-runner edits are limited to: new is_n25_validation_plan predicate; exclusion of that explicit marker from is_n25_plan and legacy is_n7_plan/is_n23_plan/is_n23_v2_plan classification; inclusion in metered_plan/typed_metered_plan; validation contract selection before Dev in metered_support; marker inclusion in the two existing E2/runtime-condition checks in validate_plan; validation budget-contract route in check_budget; validation recovery route in check_retry; validation exposure-registration hook in append_event_locked; and explicit validation dispatched-label selection in run_plan/reconcile_ledger terminal metadata. Do not modify primitive locking, subprocess/resource ownership, actual execution, metering, cleanup, timeout, provider, native arithmetic, or original Dev acceptance semantics. Report any additional needed edit before proceeding.
+
+Worker edits remain only a minimal explicit validate_context route. run_worker, verify_receipt and all other original worker functions remain byte-identical. No function-code cloning, monkey-patching or shared-global replacement. New validation code must implement its independent stricter gates rather than treating Dev acceptance as validation acceptance.
+
+Provide exact whole-file reverse replacements for every permitted shared-runner and worker insertion/change. They must reconstruct both original Dev files byte-for-byte and separately show all other255 original files unchanged. Use synthetic plans/rows to demonstrate original Dev and older routes are unchanged, validation reaches its own contract, missing/wrong markers or authority fail, original N25 native audit remains active and protected source/identity checks cannot downgrade into Dev. Root reviews this future bridge before any integration. No current running source or phase release changes.
